{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Preferences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"],"title":"Preferences","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/removeValue(for:)","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Swidux\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestore"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KeyValueStore"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps inject a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" through their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Environment"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate initial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state from it once at app start, and write to it from effects:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Environment","struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","}","","\/\/ Hydration","extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system)","    }","}","","\/\/ Reducer + effect","case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Hydration-only reads","type":"heading","anchor":"Hydration-only-reads"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reads are intended for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hydration at app start"}]},{"type":"text","text":", not mid-cycle reads from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reducers. UserDefaults itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect writes creates ordering ambiguity. Reducers that need a preference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should read it once into state and then observe state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Failures","type":"heading","anchor":"Failures"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"value(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): missing keys and decode failures both return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Decode failures are logged via "},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Encode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"setValue(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): encode failures are logged and trigger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in DEBUG. Production builds log and continue. The API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not throw — encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. "},{"code":"Float.nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an effect."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Backing store unavailable","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"setValue(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"removeValue(for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"return "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The result is "},{"code":"@discardableResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so writes that cannot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fail meaningfully stay a single line. This matters for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", where an unsigned or unentitled build cannot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reach the keychain at all. No caller can fix that, so it logs and returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead of trapping."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Schema migration","type":"heading","anchor":"Schema-migration"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" shape changes that aren’t backward-compatible should declare a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type